<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61072" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῦρος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εος</span>, τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>supreme power, authority</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἔχειν ἀμφί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					391
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν πρηγμάτων τὸ κ. ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					6.109
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅπαν τὸ κ. ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					5.38
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				450e
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἔχειν περί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Cra.</u>
					435c
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ κ. τῆς ἐνεργείας</span>
			<i>principle</i> or <i>origin</i> of a function, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				10.459
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> concrete,
				<i>one invested with authority</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				70c
			</span></i>c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>confirmation, validity</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχειν κ.,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεκυρῶσθαι</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1779
			</span></i> (anap.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				2110.12
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv A.D.)</span>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ νῦν . . ὑπάρξει κ. ἡμέρα καλῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					919
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. λαβεῖν</span>, of a law, <i>to
				be ratified</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				38.17
			</span></i>, al.:—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῦρος</span> and
			all derivs. are post-<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> (Cf. Skt. <i>śūas</i> 'valiant', OIr.
				<i>caur</i> 'hero', Welsh <i>cawr</i> 'giant'.)</div>
